\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Metamodel of the Agentic Configuration Item (ACI). The ACI constitutes the fundamental building block of the ACM reference model. The metamodel defines a common representation for governed configuration items, their specialization hierarchy (Structural, Governance, and Runtime ACIs), agentic configuration types, and governance metadata. Associated entities, including provenance records, content digests, content references, and tags, provide the information required for immutable identification, traceability, integrity verification, and reproducible configuration management.}}{11}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:aci_metamodel}{{4}{11}{Metamodel of the Agentic Configuration Item (ACI). The ACI constitutes the fundamental building block of the ACM reference model. The metamodel defines a common representation for governed configuration items, their specialization hierarchy (Structural, Governance, and Runtime ACIs), agentic configuration types, and governance metadata. Associated entities, including provenance records, content digests, content references, and tags, provide the information required for immutable identification, traceability, integrity verification, and reproducible configuration management}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{fig:aci_metamodel@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][10][]11}}
